Third-party code

src/dionw/_polar_express.py and src/dionw/_symmetric_kernels.py contain code
from microsoft/dion (https://github.com/microsoft/dion, commit 7692479), MIT
License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation: the Polar Express iteration and
the symmetric-product Triton kernels (ns_line_1, ns_line_2).

src/dionw/_gram.py contains an adaptation of Dao-AILab's Gram
Newton-Schulz (https://github.com/Dao-AILab/gram-newton-schulz), by Jack Zhang,
Noah Amsel, Berlin Chen and Tri Dao, declared MIT in its pyproject.toml (the
repository has no LICENSE file): the Gram iteration and its coefficients. Its
CuTeDSL kernels are not used.

Both are distributed under the MIT License text above. Copyright in that code
remains with its authors: Microsoft Corporation for the microsoft/dion code, and
Jack Zhang, Noah Amsel, Berlin Chen and Tri Dao for the Gram Newton-Schulz
adaptation.
